# Branded documents (email, PDF, invoice)

Off-site documents must match Ohmni identity without copying the website CSS stack.

## Source of truth

- **Document colors/fonts:** [`lib/brand-palette.ts`](lib/brand-palette.ts) (sync with `tokens/color.json` light + `tokens/font.json`)
- **Site tokens / review:** `tokens/*`, `/design`
- **Names / from-address:** [`lib/brand.ts`](lib/brand.ts)
- **Logo:** `public/ohmni.svg`

## Medium rules

- **Email** — Inline styles or `@react-email/components` under `emails/` (or update [`components/email-template`](components/email-template/index.tsx)). No Tailwind classes, no Motion, no texture heroes. CTAs = `primary` + `primaryForeground`.
- **PDF / invoice** — PDF stack or print CSS; embed Inter-compatible fonts; scannable hierarchy (logo header, bill-to, line items, totals). Not page-builder sections.
- **Don’t** invent a second palette; **do** update `brand-palette.ts` when light tokens change.

## Checklist

1. Read `brandPalette` + `brand`
2. Pick email vs PDF vs print HTML
3. Build with hex / React Email — not section shells
4. Consistent Ohmni naming + logo
5. Keep layout simple
